 observable : [à préciser].\nVérification reproductible : [commande ou parcours à préciser].\nCas d’échec et reprise : [à préciser].\nLa présence d’un rapport ou la fin d’un processus ne vaut pas acceptation.\n\n## Décisions\nRelire le brief et le plan avant autorisation. Le modèle ne préautorise aucune exécution, augmentation de budget, acceptation, publication ou fusion. Toute inconnue reste une question explicite.\n\nStructure proposée : interface v1. Les étapes proposées ne sont pas des commandes exécutées.\n\n\n12. Après la recette acceptée, proposer un RETEX et des quick wins : constat sourcé, valeur utilisateur, effort, risque et critère vérifiable. L’utilisateur choisit les évolutions à préparer ; aucune exécution implicite.\n",
+      "en": "# Create or improve an interface\n\nUser journey and screen involved: [describe them].\nWhy and for whom: [describe it].\nAuthorised scope: [define it].\nOut of scope: [define it].\nConstraints and budget: [define them; no preauthorised limits].\n\n## Proposed workflow\nRequirements framing → Research → Interface design → Planning → Implementation → Review → Delivery. Design applies only when a user interface is involved.\n\n## Expected organisation\nA planner owns the need; add subplanners only for justified scopes. Workers deliver tasks; an independent review examines their results. Define dependencies, workspaces, owners and limits before launch.\n\n## Methods by role\n- Planner : Analysis and planning — frame the need only. Define tasks, criteria and dependencies; no implementation or approval of its own plan.\n- Workers : Implementation and verification — analyse, implement and verify the authorised task. Return evidence; its checks do not replace independent review.\n- Independent reviewer : Independent review — examine evidence and propose corrections. Do not implement corrections; only the engine decides acceptance.\nMethods are included by the engine according to role. Preparation allows analysis and planning only. A subplanner retains planner boundaries. A method grants no additional permission.\n\nExamine and improve: prepare → implement → verify → improve. Each role remains within its assignment.\n\n## Deliverables and evidence\nApproved brief; research with sources; justified design when relevant; plan with bounded tasks; result and reproducible checks; review report; prepared delivery. For a new product, add a PRD and stories before the plan.\n\n## Criteria to complete\nObservable behaviour: [define it].\nReproducible verification: [define a command or user journey].\nFailure and recovery cases: [define them].\nA report's presence or a process ending does not constitute acceptance.\n\n## Decisions\nReview the brief and plan before authorising work. This template does not authorise execution, budget increases, acceptance, publication or merge. Keep unknowns as explicit questions.\n\nProposed structure: interface v1. Proposed steps are not executed commands.\n\n\n12. After an accepted recipe, offer a retrospective and quick wins: sourced observation, user value, effort, risk and a verifiable criterion. The user chooses which evolutions to prepare; no implicit execution.\n"
