ithin its assignment.\n\n## Deliverables and evidence\nApproved brief; research with sources; justified design when relevant; plan with bounded tasks; result and reproducible checks; review report; prepared delivery. For a new product, add a PRD and stories before the plan.\n\n## Proposed outcome\nA reproducible exchange that respects permissions, format and recovery.\n\n## Example to adapt\nSynchronise orders between a website and a management tool.\n\n## Proposed deliverables\n- Versioned contract and examples\n- Authentication and error handling\n- Recovery and compatibility strategy\n\n## Evidence to plan\n- Real valid and invalid requests\n- Denial without permission\n- Replay without duplicate effects and a simulated outage\n\n## Risks to examine\n- Duplicate effects\n- Contract breakage\n- Secrets in logs\n\n## Decisions\nReview the brief and plan before authorising work. This template does not authorise execution, budget increases, acceptance, publication or merge. Keep unknowns as explicit questions.\n\n\n\n12. After an accepted recipe, offer a retrospective and quick wins: sourced observation, user value, effort, risk and a verifiable criterion. The user chooses which evolutions to prepare; no implicit execution.\n"
